  <p>
    Neither track is objectively better. The honest deciding question is not "which one sounds more
    creative," because they all use real design judgment. It is: does visual communication for brands and
    print genuinely interest you more, or does the behaviour and functionality of a digital product pull you
    in more, or does movement and short-form storytelling energise you more? Answer that honestly before the
    word "design" answers it for you. For the deeper skill-overlap, salary, and freelance-viability
